IMPORT prelude

-- A paired `MAYBE NUMBER` INSIDE a gathered list element.
--
-- The §8.4 changed-answer repair clears a gated answer by putting `undefine:`
-- on the question that gates it. That does not reach inside a gather, and the
-- reason is a docassemble asymmetry: `ask` runs `substitute_vars` over
-- `reconsider:` and NOT over `undefine:` (parse.py:5389 beside :5392 at
-- 1b6678384), so a `<list>[i].<attr>` spelling would arrive at `undefine()`
-- with the iterator unresolved.
--
-- So the emitter emits no `undefine:` on an element question, and declares the
-- omission as `DA-UNDEFINE-LIST` rather than leaving it silent. Expect: the
-- element's is-known flag question carries `show if:` on the value question but
-- NO `undefine:` anywhere carrying `[i]`, and the fidelity report names the
-- gated element variable.

DECLARE Claimant
    HAS
      @desc The claimant's name
      `the name`         IS A STRING
      @desc The claimant's declared income, if they gave one
      `declared income`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER

DECLARE Household
    HAS
      @desc Everyone claiming in this household
      claimants IS A LIST OF Claimant

@export whether every claimant declared an income above the threshold
GIVEN h IS A Household @desc The household under assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the household is above the threshold` h IF
    all (GIVEN c YIELD `the claimant is above the threshold` c) (h's claimants)

GIVEN c IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant is above the threshold` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `declared income`
    WHEN JUST amount THEN amount AT LEAST 1000
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN FALSE

#EVAL `the household is above the threshold` OF
        Household WITH
            claimants IS LIST
                Claimant WITH `the name` IS "A", `declared income` IS JUST 2000
-- TRUE
